XORing something twice with the same value cancels it out.  
  
  A xor B xor B = A
  
- XOR encryption and decryption are the same operation.  
      - Ciphertext = Plaintext XOR Key  
      - Plaintext = Ciphertext XOR Key  

Because XOR undoes itself, using the same key again restores the original data.

